b + 1 )\n\nBut we also have a\u00b2 = (d - 1 )\u00b2 + e\u00b2\n\nBut since b\u00b2 = d\u00b2 + e\u00b2, so e\u00b2 = b\u00b2 - d\u00b2\n\nTherefore,\n\na\u00b2 = (d - 1 )\u00b2 + b\u00b2 - d\u00b2 = d\u00b2 - 2d + 1 + b\u00b2 - d\u00b2 = b\u00b2 - 2d + 1\n\nBut d = b/(b + 1 )\n\nTherefore,\n\na\u00b2 = b\u00b2 - 2*(b/(b + 1 )) + 1 = b\u00b2 - (2b)/(b + 1 ) + 1\n\nTherefore,\n\na\u00b2 = b\u00b2 + 1 - (2b)/(b + 1 )\n\nNow, let's substitute this into the acuteness conditions.\n\nFirst condition: a\u00b2 < b\u00b2 + 1\n\nFrom above, a\u00b2 = b\u00b2 + 1 - (2b)/(b + 1 )\n\nTherefore,\n\nb\u00b2 + 1 - (2b)/(b + 1 ) < b\u00b2 + 1\n\nSubtract b\u00b2 + 1:\n\n- (2b)/(b + 1 ) < 0\n\nWhich is true since b > 0.\n\nSecond condition: b\u00b2 < a\u00b2 + 1\n\nFrom a\u00b2 = b\u00b2 + 1 - (2b)/(b + 1 )\n\nThus,\n\nb\u00b2 < [b\u00b2 + 1 - (2b)/(b + 1 ) ] + 1\n\nSimplify RHS:\n\nb\u00b2 + 1 - (2b)/(b + 1 ) + 1 = b\u00b2 + 2 - (2b)/(b + 1 )\n\nTherefore,\n\nb\u00b2 < b\u00b2 + 2 - (2b)/(b + 1 )\n\nSubtract b\u00b2:\n\n0 < 2 - (2b)/(b + 1 )\n\nWhich is equivalent to:\n\n(2b)/(b + 1 ) < 2\n\nMultiply both sides by (b + 1 ):\n\n2b < 2(b + 1 )\n\nSimplify:\n\n2b < 2b + 2\n\nSubtract 2b:\n\n0 < 2\n\nWhich is always true.\n\nThird condition: a\u00b2 + b\u00b2 > 1\n\nFrom a\u00b2 = b\u00b2 + 1 - (2b)/(b + 1 )\n\nThus,\n\na\u00b2 + b\u00b2 = 2b\u00b2 + 1 - (2b)/(b + 1 )\n\nNeed to show:\n\n2b\u00b2 + 1 - (2b)/(b + 1 ) > 1\n\nSubtract 1:\n\n2b\u00b2 - (2b)/(b + 1 ) > 0\n\nFactor out 2b:\n\n2b [ b - 1/(b + 1 ) ] > 0\n\nSince b > 0, we need:\n\nb - 1/(b + 1 ) > 0\n\nWhich is equivalent to:\n\nb(b + 1 ) - 1 > 0\n\n=> b\u00b2 + b - 1 > 0\n\nWhich, as before, has roots at b = [ -1 \u00b1 sqrt(5 ) ]/2. The positive root is (sqrt(5 ) - 1 )/2 \u2248 0.618.\n\nTherefore, b > (sqrt(5 ) - 1 )/2 \u2248 0.618\n\nThus, the third acuteness condition requires that b > (sqrt(5 ) - 1 )/2, which is approximately 0.618. As established earlier, this implies that cos \u03b1 = 1/(b + 1 ) < 1/(0.618 + 1 ) \u2248 